{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce6rNjETTcT1gBCXy5Vxi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YTPhJwnEiPsMnHsyZxHtSG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ns/workspace/dpt-test-project-jira/specs/plan/M_DST_74.md","content":"---\nmilestone: M_DST_74\nstatus: active\narchived_at: null\nkickoff_branch: null\nfrozen_at: null\nmigration: none\n---\n\n# Implementation Plan\n\n## Milestone Order\n\n<!-- Each milestone gets its own `specs/plan/M<N>.md` file -->\n<!-- Don't proceed to the next milestone until this one's gates pass -->\n\n### Task Sizing\n\nEach task should be ≈ one commit's worth of work — small enough that the verification step is unambiguous. Write tasks as 2-line entries:\n\n- line 1 — the action as a checkbox bullet, e.g. `- [ ] Add X`\n- line 2 — an indented `verify:` line stating the command or observation that proves the task is done\n\nIf you can't write the `verify:` line in one sentence, the task is too big. Split it.\n\nA task may also be marked `[deferred]` (e.g., `- [deferred] multiply — moved to the next milestone`) to signal that the work was intentionally moved out of this milestone. `/ship-milestone` treats `[deferred]` as ship-OK and `/gate-check` skips it from the task-FR coverage probe.\n\n## M_DST_74 — Gate command and tooling versions documented {#M_DST_74}\n\n**Goal:** Record the repository's canonical gate command and the tooling versions it runs on in `specs/technical-spec.md`, so the verification contract lives in the technical spec rather than being reconstructed from `CLAUDE.md` plus two scattered tables.\n**Prerequisites:** M1 (bootstrap) — the gate command and the tooling it names must already exist and be green.\n\n**FR list:**\n\n| FR | Title | Tracker |\n|----|-------|---------|\n| DST-75 | tooling-and-gate — record the canonical gate command and its tooling versions in the technical spec | [DST-75](https://stellartechlab.atlassian.net/browse/DST-75) |\n\n**Tasks:**\n- [ ] Add a `## 7. Tooling & Gate` section to `specs/technical-spec.md`, placed after `## 6. Risks & Considerations` and before the `## Architecture Decision Records` table, recording the gate command verbatim in a fenced block plus the line naming `CLAUDE.md` § Gating rule as its source of truth\n  verify: `grep -F 'bunx tsc --noEmit && bun test' specs/technical-spec.md` matches, and the matched string is byte-identical to the `Gating rule` line in `CLAUDE.md` (AC-DST-75.1)\n- [ ] Add the three-row tooling-versions table to that same section, pairing each tool with its version and the declaration site the value was read from\n  verify: the section lists Bun `1.3.14`, TypeScript `5.9.3`, and `@types/bun` `latest`, each with a non-empty \"Declared at\" cell (AC-DST-75.2)\n\n**Tests:**\n- None. The deliverable is Markdown prose in a spec file — no exported function, no module boundary, no behaviour to assert. `specs/frs/DST-75.md` § Testing records why a grep-the-spec test would pin wording rather than behaviour.\n- `src/.placeholder.test.ts` stays in place: this milestone lands no real test file, and `bun test` exits 1 on zero matches.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] AC-DST-75.1: `specs/technical-spec.md` records the gate command verbatim as `bunx tsc --noEmit && bun test`, byte-identical to the `Gating rule` line in `CLAUDE.md`\n- [ ] AC-DST-75.2: `specs/technical-spec.md` records the tooling versions the gate runs on — Bun `1.3.14`, TypeScript `5.9.3`, and `@types/bun` `latest` — each paired with its declaration site\n\n**Gate:** `bunx tsc --noEmit && bun test`\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":118169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1787},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_manageme