the gate is the one string every downstream skill (`/gate-check`, `/tdd`, `/implement`, `/ship-milestone`) shells out to.\n\n**Part 2 — tooling versions** (AC-DST-75.2): a three-row table pairing each tool with its version and, critically, the declaration site the value was read from.\n\n| Tool | Version | Declared at |\n|------|---------|-------------|\n| Bun | `1.3.14` | `bun.lock` / project stack contract |\n| TypeScript | `5.9.3` | resolved from the `typescript` `^5` peer range in `package.json` |\n| `@types/bun` | `latest` | `devDependencies` in `package.json` |\n\nThe \"Declared at\" column is what keeps the section honest. Two of the three values are *resolved*, not *pinned* — `^5` and `latest` are ranges, so the recorded `5.9.3` is an observation of today's resolution rather than a guarantee. Recording where each came from tells a future reader which numbers can move under them without any file in this repository changing.\n\nBoth parts are written at the section's top level, not nested inside a numbered list. Block-level content nested in a list item does not survive this project's Markdown-to-ADF round trip — the first push of this FR lost the table that way, silently and with a success-shaped response, which is the documented trap `specs/technical-spec.md` § 4 names. Keeping tables flush-left keeps the tracker copy faithful to this file."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7604,"cache_read_input_tokens":121469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7604},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52db325d-f99d-4924-9257-a07a3d9431f6","uuid":"3f39786e-1096-4643-8c48-2954285573a5","timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:52:34.338Z","request_id":"req_011Ce6rSJpt93q34kcby8mWH"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce6rTsjpDk6Eib122fy6D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UAmibF7D1fv2sn97DLSE6V","name":"mcp__atlassian__editJiraIssue","input":{"cloudId":"96bffaef-cf5d-4dbf-a170-3d700df9bc83","issueIdOrKey":"DST-75","contentFormat":"markdown","fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAnyone joining this repository has to reconstruct how a change is verified from two places, and neither of them is the technical specification.\nThe command that must pass before anything merges is written down only in the project contract file, while the versions of the runtime and the type checker that command depends on sit scattered across a design-decisions table and a dependencies table.\nA reader who wants to know what green means, and on which tooling, has to stitch three fragments together and trust that none of them has drifted from the others.\nThis change records both facts in the technical specification itself, as one named contract that can be checked at a glance.\nIt is documentation only — no source module, no test, and no build setting is touched.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a **Tooling & Gate** section to `specs/technical-spec.md` that records two things: (a) the repository's canonical gate command, verbatim, and (b) the versions of the tooling that command runs on. The section is additive prose plus a table; no source file, test file, or build configuration is modified by this FR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC-DST-75.1: `specs/technical-spec.md` records the gate command verbatim as `bunx tsc --noEmit && bun test` — byte-identical to the `Gating rule` line in `CLAUDE.md`, with no paraphrase, no reordering of the two halves, and no substitution of `bun x` or `npx` for `bunx`.\n- [ ] AC-DST-75.2: `specs/technical-spec.md` records the tooling versions the gate runs on — Bun `1.3.14`, TypeScript `5.9.3` (the version `bunx tsc` resolves from the `typescript` `^5` peer range), and `@types/bun` at `latest` — each paired with the declaration site the value came from.\n\n## Technical Design\n\nThe change edits one existing file, `specs/technical-spec.md`, and adds no code.\n\nA new `## 7. Tooling & Gate` section lands after `## 6. Risks & Considerations` and before the `## Architecture Decision Records` table, so the numbered sections stay contiguous and the ADR table remains the file's trailing block.\n\nThe section carries two parts, one per acceptance criterion.\n\n**Part 1 — gate command** (AC-DST-75.1): the command in a fenced block, plus one line naming `CLAUDE.md` § Gating rule as the source it must stay byte-identical to. Recording it verbatim rather than describing it is the point: a paraphrase cannot be diffed against the contract file, and the gate is the one string every downstream skill (`/gate-check`, `/tdd`, `/implement`, `/ship-milestone`) shells out to.\n\n**Part 2 — tooling versions** (AC-DST-75.2): a three-row table pairing each tool with its version and, critically, the declaration site the value was read from.\n\n| Tool | Version | Declared at |\n|------|---------|-------------|\n| Bun | `1.3.14` | `bun.lock` / project stack contract |\n| TypeScript | `5.9.3` | resolved from the `typescript` `^5` peer range in `package.json` |\n| `@types/bun` | `latest` | `devDependencies` in `package.json` |\n\nThe \"Declared at\" column is what keeps the section honest. Two of the three values are *resolved*, not *pinned* — `^5` and `latest` are ranges, so the recorded `5.9.3` is an observation of today's resolution rather than a guarantee. Recording where each came from tells a future reader which numbers can move under them without any file in this repository changing.\n\nBoth parts are written at the section's top level, not nested inside a numbered list. Block-level content nested in a list item does not survive this project's Markdown-to-ADF round trip — the first push of this FR lost the table that way, silently and with a success-shaped response, which is the documented trap `specs/technical-spec.md` § 4 names. Keeping tables flush-left keeps the tracker copy faithful to this file.\n\nExisting content is not relocated. Bun `1.3.14` already appears in the § 1 Key Design Decisions table and the two dependency rows already appear in § 5; those stay where they are. This FR adds the consolidated gate contract, it does not refactor the spec — deleting the originals would widen a documentation FR into an edit of two unrelated sections.\n\nPer `specs/technical-spec.md` § 4, nothing here has an error path: the deliverable is prose, and its correctness is checked by reading, not by a runtime assertion.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new tests. The deliverable is a Markdown section in a spec file; there is no exported function, no module boundary, and no behaviour to assert. Writing a test that greps a spec file for its own prose would pin the wording, not the behaviour, and would fail on any harmless rewording — the anti-pattern `specs/testing-spec.md` § 3 (What NOT to Test) already names.\n\nThe obligation this FR carries instead is that the existing gate stays green:\n\n```\nbunx tsc --noEmit && bun test\n```\n\nmust still exit 0 after the edit, exactly as before it. Since no `.ts` file is touched, `tsc` has nothing new to check and `bun test` runs the same suite; a red gate after this FR would mean something outside its stated scope was modified.\n\n`src/.placeholder.test.ts` is **not** deleted by this FR. It may only be removed in the same commit that lands the first real test file (`CLAUDE.md` § DO NOT, `specs/testing-spec.md` § 2), and this FR lands none — `bun test` exits 1 on zero matches, so deleting it here would break the gate for every downstream skill.\n\nVerification for both ACs is a read of the resulting `specs/technical-spec.md`: AC-DST-75.1 is satisfied when the recorded command string matches `CLAUDE.md`'s byte for byte, AC-DST-75.2 when all three tool/version/declaration-site rows are present.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nAny source-code change. Specifically: no edit to `index.ts`, no new or modified file under `src/`, no change to `package.json`, `bun.lock`, or `tsconfig.json`, and no change to the gate command itself — this FR records the command that exists, it does not redefine it. Also out of scope: pinning the `typescript` range or the `@types/bun` `latest` tag to exact versions (a real dependency-policy decision, and a `package.json` edit this FR is not authorised to make), adding CI configuration to enforce the gate, and relocating the pre-existing version mentions out of § 1 and § 5.\n\n## Notes\n\nMilestone `M_DST_74` is realised as Jira Epic `DST-74` (canonical name `M_DST_74 — Gate command and tooling versions documented`); this Task binds to it via its `parent` field. The milestone id is derived from the Epic key via `milestoneIdFromEpicKey` (`DST-74` → `M_DST_74`), so the five-way `nextFreeMilestoneNumber` scan is bypassed on the Jira path.\n\nThe two resolved-not-pinned versions are the standing hazard in this FR. `typescript: ^5` and `@types/bun: latest` both float, so AC-DST-75.2's recorded `5.9.3` is true as of the drafting run and can go stale without any commit to this repository. That is why the acceptance criterion requires the declaration site alongside the version rather than the bare number — the number is an observation, the declaration site is the durable fact. If a future FR pins the ranges, this section's table becomes exact and the caveat can be dropped.\n\nBranch type for this FR derives to `feat` via `branchTypeFor({ changelogCategory: \"Changed\" })`, which is keyed on the changelog category rather than the commit type. The drafting session specified `chore` as the commit type for the eventual implementation commit; the two are independent and both stand — flagged here because the mismatch looks like drift and is not.\n\n---\n\nSource: specs/frs/DST-75.md"}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1866,"cache_read_input_tokens":129073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1866},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52db325d-f99d-4924-9257-a07a3d9431f6","uuid":"a3fdd64e-131c-40d9-a8b7-a38cdfac991e","timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:53:04.801Z","request_id":"req_011Ce6rTrnX668Qv5z1p2Lc5","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UAmibF7D1fv2sn97DLSE6V","display_name":"Update issue","server_display_name":"atlassian-mcp-server"}]}
